{"ld": 1782, "paper": "HP1193", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Regarding Host Community Compensation for the Juniper Ridge Landfill in the City of Old Town (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-dill-james", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-campbell-richard", "h-hepler-allison", "h-osher-laurie", "s-tipping-michael"], "committee_code": "ENR", "committee_name": "Environment and Natural Resources", "summary": {"text": "This bill updates the Juniper Ridge Landfill host community compensation agreement and adequately compensates the City of Old Town for hosting the largest state-owned landfill. It further directs the Department of Administrative and Financial Services, Bureau of General Services and the Department of Environmental Protection to immediately investigate and address, through preparation of a solid waste management plan, several critical issues and developments in the State's solid waste management system involving the Juniper Ridge Landfill in the City of Old Town that have converged to create a crisis for approximately 159 central and northern municipalities and for sewer and utility districts and departments all across the State. The bill applies the same terms to other state-owned or state-operated landfills in the State.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1193&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-10", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-10"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1782)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1193&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-408)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1193&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-408)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & 